    {
      "id": "emergent_compute_black_market",
      "description": "An underground market in access to high-capability AI systems emerges, leveraging compromised academic and corporate cloud accounts, forged credentials, and repurposed public infrastructure. These services offer near-frontier capability to non-state actors, researchers, and rogue developers outside official channels, bypassing export controls and usage monitoring. The network is resilient, decentralized, and difficult to trace, marking a structural shift in access distribution.",
